{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/307001-mortal-alchemist-demiurge","id":307001,"title":"Mortal Alchemist Demiurge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-08T16:05:23-08:00","id":307001,"title":"Mortal Alchemist Demiurge?","content":"How hard (or unbalancing) would it be to allow a player to be a mortal demiurge? Could a demiurge stay with his/her creations while on their pilgrimages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T00:52:56-08:00","id":307250,"title":"","content":"Well it depends on what you mean by &quot;mortal alchemist.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you mean a plain mortal who manages to midwife a new promethean into the world, they wouldn't be immune to disquiet.<br /> <br /> If you are talking about an alchemist like the antagonists they will introduce in the new book, we don't know if they have a cure for disquiet in their bag of tricks, and what with prometheans being walking talking alchemical ingredients, that doesn't really suggest a healthy relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T10:01:36-08:00","id":307534,"title":"","content":"Nothing inherently unbalanced, but Demiurges have no inherent immunity to Disquiet, and are as if not more prone to become obsessed with/hateful of/hanted by (etc) their Creation than others they encounter. Just look at the anatagonist relationships in most of the source materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T10:26:21-08:00","id":308329,"title":"","content":"So, I personally think that having a human being, even one who nominally understands the Promethean condition, tagging along on the Pilgrimage is kinda counter to the themes of <b>Promethean</b>, and logistically, you'd run into Disquiet issues. <br /> <br /> With that said? That's totally just, like, my opinion, man. I can see it working and doing some interesting things in a story, and there's nothing inherently game-breaking about it that I can think of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T15:07:30-08:00","id":308538,"title":"","content":"IMHO, mortal demiurges open up whole new story options that are consistent with <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s themes, but don\u2019t fit the standard model of \u201cmonsters stumbling around in the dark, trying to find their way on their own\u201d. Going with the notion that <b>Promethean</b> is an allegory for childhood and growing up, mortal demiurges play the role of the parent \u2014 the grown-up authority figure who\u2019s there to guide and protect. This being the World of Darkness, though, such relationships are rarely clean: even setting aside the effects of Disquiet, to which demiurges have no special immunity, there ought to be a tension between parents and children. In general, it\u2019s a role that works better as supporting cast than as another protagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T15:40:00-08:00","id":308579,"title":"","content":"In the prologue of Promethean, one of the characters reveals himself as Dr. Frankenstein\u00b4s monster. It is implied the doctor was a normal human playing weird science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T15:51:26-08:00","id":308584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/307001-mortal-alchemist-demiurge?p=308579#post308579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the prologue of Promethean, one of the characters reveals himself as Dr. Frankenstein\u00b4s monster. It is implied the doctor was a normal human playing weird science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what a Demiurge is. It's extremely narratively important that Doctor Frankenstein was horrified byand abandoned his Creation, setting the Monster on a course of vengeance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-10-2014, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T15:56:51-08:00","id":308589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/307001-mortal-alchemist-demiurge?p=308538#post308538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, mortal demiurges open up whole new story options that are consistent with <b>Promethean</b>\u2019s themes, but don\u2019t fit the standard model of \u201cmonsters stumbling around in the dark, trying to find their way on their own\u201d. Going with the notion that <b>Promethean</b> is an allegory for childhood and growing up, mortal demiurges play the role of the parent \u2014 the grown-up authority figure who\u2019s there to guide and protect. This being the World of Darkness, though, such relationships are rarely clean: even setting aside the effects of Disquiet, to which demiurges have no special immunity, there ought to be a tension between parents and children. In general, it\u2019s a role that works better as supporting cast than as another protagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you want to explore the allegory of parenthood from a PC perspective, Promethean Creators do that far better than Mortal Demiurges, as it fits their own &quot;learning to be human&quot; arc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T17:32:24-08:00","id":308663,"title":"","content":"Actually, the fact that they\u2019re still learning to be human makes it more of a \u201cteen mothers\u201d thing \u2014 that is, kids raising kids. So it\u2019s very much <i>not</i> a better way to approach the parent/child dynamic in general. Using demiurges as authority figures for the Created addresses a wide variety of story possibilities that just aren\u2019t there without them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: sorry; I missed the \u201cfrom a PC perspective\u201d. You\u2019re right about that part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}